mped positions\n\nReason: d7-d5 is the best move because it opens up Black's cramped position, activates the dark-squared bishop, and fights for central control. This pawn break is critical to get Black's pieces into the game and create counterplay against White's active knights. Without opening the position, Black will remain cramped with no prospects.\n\nAnswer: P: d7-d5"}
